{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: the complete 157-subject I1 candidate at a3e5a77eb28e91e1a0458af0526eea446387b7c4, direct parent ebad6f0cd66bc56f85f4313ca52e37b2a560c89b. Independent ordinary source review against the prior FULL 34d3b656 review and the exact-head preliminary bdb76a9a found both P2 findings from 82690f74 repaired, with no remaining material blocker established. This approves this scope-substrate source delivery; the full platform and separately owned dependent deliveries remain owed.\n\nCanonical actor and signature: records.ts:115/118 now use the shared key/signature guards. ids.ts:21–27 checks the canonical 32-byte key and 64-byte signature forms, including the unchanged decoder's rejection of noncanonical trailing bits. A malformed actor can no longer pass the nested fixed-record check merely because it is text. This is structural validation; it does not replace signature verification, independent receipt proof or authority.\n\nExpired and late reads: take.ts:55–80 checks the exchange state before starting a read and before retaining its result, drops held chunks at expiry, rejects late chunks, attempts cancellation without waiting for an uncooperative reader, and never retains empty chunks. Empty immediate reads yield to the timer queue. The client and replay callers check LATE before joining their decoding/parsing paths. A response arriving after expiry is cancelled without starting its reads. A Fetch or stream that ignores abort can retain its own buffers or connection; the delivery explicitly qualifies that boundary. Unknown submitted intents remain unknown and use exact retry/settlement, rather than being reported as not recorded.\n\nArchitecture: shared byte, identifier and fixed-record guards and one bounded reader keep the transport/replay boundary in one place. The other 140 source/document subjects are byte-identical to the prior complete source review. Scope-local storage and turn transactions, shared pure derivation, independent history verification, finite due-first timed work, explicit duty reserves, retained inputs, exact retry/settlement, source-owned delivery/relationships and honest missing/incomplete reads remain intact. The earlier timer-graph, consumed-input/evidence, byte-bound, signing-snapshot and reference-identity repairs are not reversed. All 157 dated source choices remain recorded, with adoption distinct from implementation.\n\nSecurity: production authority and read ports remain refusing defaults. Test authority is not made available through the production entrypoint. Real grants, freshness/membership, founding policy, platform definitions, read sessions, hold/fork/token/export and outside effect evidence remain I3 or other named dependent work. Shape validation is not cryptographic verification or a public proof of a receipt. Source approval adopts no later design delta and proves no provider, device, custody, browser or publication behavior.\n\nSimplification and removal: the six active packages retain one canonical/encoding/signing implementation and one reply reader. Active/parked boundaries, scripts, manifests, configuration, guides and the replacement ledger remain covered. Against the previously reviewed main b2a0bb12 snapshot, the 157 ordinary subjects retain their complete additions/modifications/partial-renames; the pure moves and deletions have unchanged custody/removal evidence. Deferred I2/I3/I5 successors remain owned and are removed when replaced; parked historical material is not an active second runtime. No legacy adapter, new engine, duplicate suite, numerical quota or first-Jam gate is introduced.\n\nExisting nonblocking follow-through remains open. Repeated races against the pending expiry promise retain bookkeeping proportional to read count; consider a removable wait or one whole-loop expiry race in the existing reader work. Immediately resolved nonempty reads have normal timer-scheduling limits; no actual default-30-second failure or strict CPU-time guarantee was established. The existing 48030ca2/520ebceb controlled-scheduler and test-economy duties remain: replace the new real 1/5/10/30/40 ms waits in client/replay witnesses with controlled timers and explicit resolutions while preserving unknown-intent, nonawaited cancellation, no late read/response/chunk, empty-progress and timeout-before-decode boundaries. This is not a new production P2, request, suite or approval gate. reserve.ts:9–10 still mixes “adopted since” with “not adopted yet”; correct the historical comment in existing follow-through. Delivery references to retired 108ea663 and later R1 adoption status need the existing owner reconciliation, without claiming that this source implements the successor's eight must-change rows.\n\nEvidence limits: the builder reports typecheck and 205 tests passing in about five seconds at this head. That is attributed producer evidence; checker did not execute it. The earlier warm-cache, shared-machine main-versus-c2ea17ce cost columns compare different products and cannot show a tenfold useful-work gain. Comparable complete install-to-review costs and the highest-priority useful-test economy remain owed with later deliveries. The executable's declared Node range is not independent proof of execution on every supported release. The evaluator's retained earlier corpus and later meaningful boundary proofs remain explicitly owned.\n\nCoverage: FULL current invitation text/body/decision, original 2186c3c2 commission, own promise and primary artifact inspected by checker; prepare binds this delivery to 2186c3c2 under aa78f7f5 with all 157 subjects and primary d97f735b first. Five readers fully inspected all 157 newly filed artifact statements, bodies and effective decisions. Their exact path/artifact/blob/byte/LF/SHA ledgers reconcile without duplicates, mismatches or gaps against checker's independently fetched immutable current bodies/metadata. Total 1,827,038 bytes / 30,130 LF. Groups: scope plus two archived guides 37 subjects; derive 35; bytes/client/contract/replay 59; other documents/config/public scripts 24; two delivery/delta notes. All 140 unchanged complete byte bodies were compared against prior FULL reads before transfer. All 17 changed current bodies and every changed-byte hunk, removal and context were FULL-read through EOF, including truncation recovery. Checker personally reread the complete delivery and current shared reader/client boundary and had personally FULL-read current records/ids/replay and affected contexts in the preliminary review. Complete 34d3→a3 U3 diff: 69,803 bytes / 680 LF, +265/-75, SHA256 57bc88f7487fff6de6444eec929cf66b7973b6889133c0f9a050a7684e50b224. Whole coverage is collective, with verified incremental transfers; it is not a claim that every reader freshly read every current body.\n\nStatic review only: no tests/build/install/typecheck, repository imports or script execution, private diagnostics, evaluator/probe/provider calls, source edits, merges, pushes or deployment. Six private cloud-review script bodies remain unopened. Builder ratification, originating requester delivery/acceptance and landing are separate acts. Schedule estimates do not constrain the complete functional scope.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d97f735b7a3e849d4812f27a21b272cc18623629","binding":"assigned","head":"a3e5a77eb28e91e1a0458af0526eea446387b7c4","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bf2be39fce4abde83adfda7b3b936fa9cdd79062\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:aa78f7f5901a4f384965c2031f680f7eaaa68d05\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01418f3a9b9739027217c71e83060ae2a0c1a40c","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}